From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 05:41:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00405/11171] [conductor] VALIDATE the .346 Anomaly-Escalation
 classifier (scripts/anomaly_escalation_classifier.py) against the historical
 retro/result corpus: run it over a representative sample of past artifacts
 (operational_retro_*.json + a spread of result artifacts) and measure (a) the
 false-escalation rate on clean bounded negatives (it must NOT escalate
 planned kill-gates), (b) that it CORRECTLY flags the known frame-violating
 cases (the P1 v1/v2 positive-control failures), (c) it never recommends
 relaxing verification. Recommend-only validation; conductor unmodified.
 Strengthens the P3 process upgrade with real-corpus evidence before the
 operator wires it in.

Automated research step by research conductor.
Task ID: exp3791-anomaly-escalation-classifier-validation

Co-Authored-By: Gemini CLI <noreply@google.com>
